title: readme

Adds an ''Equation'' button to the tiddler editor toolbar that opens the CodeCogs Equation
Editor. It opens on the maths view; ''LaTeX markup'' and ''Inline'' are toggles in its bottom
bar, next to ''Insert as'', which writes the equation at the cursor either as MathML or as an
`<img>` rendered by latex.codecogs.com.

Put your fxTeX Pro licence key, from https://fxeditor.codecogs.com/purchase, in
`$:/config/codecogs/eqneditor/Licence`. The editor loads from `fxtex.codecogs.com` at runtime -
override the host with `$:/config/codecogs/eqneditor/Server` (a host, or a full origin such as
`http://localhost:8010`) and the rendering host with `$:/config/codecogs/eqneditor/RenderUrl` if
needed.
